Words=When peace like a river attendeth my way,/nWhen sorrows like sea billows roll;/nWhatever my lot, Thou hast taught me to say,/nIt is well, it is well with my soul./tIt is well with my soul,/nIt is well, it is well with my soul./tThough Satan should buffet, though trials should come,/nLet this blest assurance control,/nThat Christ has regarded my helpless estate,/nAnd hath shed His own blood for my soul.
